  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform rod of length $L$ pivoted at one end $P$ is freely rotated in a horizontal plane with an angular velocity $\\omega$ about a vertical axis passing through $\\mathrm{P}$. If the temperature of the system is increased by $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}$, angular velocity becomes $\\frac{\\omega}{2}$. If coefficient of linear expansion of the rod is $\\alpha(\\alpha< < 1)$, then $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "95js9",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\alpha}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ortNY",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 \\alpha}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SZfiQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4 \\alpha}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y878N",
      "text": "$\\alpha$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{I} \\omega=\\mathrm{I}_{1} \\frac{\\omega}{2}$\r\n$\\quad \\mathrm{I}_{1}=2 \\mathrm{I}$\r\n$\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{ml}_{1}^{2}}{3}=2 \\frac{\\mathrm{ml}_{0}^{2}}{3}$\r\n$\\left\\{\\mathrm{I}_{0}^{2}(1+\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T})\\right\\}^{2}=2 \\mathrm{I}_{0}^{2}, \\therefore 1+2 \\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T}=2 \\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{T}=\\frac{1}{2 \\alpha}$",
